5,1,1,talk,Servas,,"Welcome, everyone. To ensure our choice is sustainable, I believe we must look at the outcomes of the last three internal rollouts and the record of cross-unit standardization efforts. Let us learn from the past to build the future.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think we should be careful about the costs. I'd like to look into the capital budget and software allowance, and also the vendor licence pricing versus fixed-fee work. I'm worried about hidden expenses.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Sakura,,I want to know if we can actually get into the buildings! I'll check the network coverage at customer plants and the staffing of the coordination group. Let's make sure we aren't just guessing!,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,I believe we need to focus on actual operational failures. I will look into the misrouted deliveries in the incident logs and the time lost to copying existing records to see where we are truly losing efficiency.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Asuka,,"I agree that operational efficiency is key, but we cannot ignore the human cost. I will look into in-house developer availability and the handling of vendor queries to assess if we actually have the capacity to implement anything.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Servas,,"It is heartening to see such diverse perspectives. @Daisuke, your caution regarding costs is wise, and @Asuka, your focus on our people is essential. Balance is the key to any enduring success.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Daisuke,,Thank you... I just don't want us to agree on something that we can't actually afford later. I'm worried that the budget might not be as clear as it seems on paper.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Sakura,,"Exactly! It's like planning a big party but forgetting to check if the door is locked! If we can't even get the network to work at the plants, the fancy software won't do anything, right?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Sakura, that is a fair point. However, we must also quantify the daily waste. If we only focus on technical barriers, we might overlook the systemic errors that are already draining our productivity every single day.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, quantifying waste is useful, but implementing a solution to fix it requires actual man-hours. If we ignore current staffing levels, we are simply shifting the burden from one inefficiency to another.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Servas,,"Wisdom often lies in the intersection of these concerns. If we align our historical lessons with @Asuka's capacity and @Ryuji's operational gaps, we shall find a path that is both practical and lasting.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I agree. I just hope we can find a project that doesn't create a financial burden for next year. I'll do my best to see if the budget sources are actually secure.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Sakura,,"Hehe, you guys are so serious! But that's why I'm here to keep things exciting! I'll make sure we don't trip over any hidden traps before we even start. Let's find something that actually works!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Sakura, excitement is fine, but precision is better. I am less interested in ""traps"" and more interested in the measurable losses we accept as normal. We must prioritize the project that solves the most frequent practical problems.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Asuka,,Precision is only possible if the people executing the plan aren't already overwhelmed. I will focus on whether we have the actual bandwidth to support a new rollout without breaking our current operations.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Servas,,"Let us proceed with these investigations. By combining our insights on history, finance, infrastructure, waste, and capacity, we will ensure our final choice is not merely a dream, but a sustainable reality. I look forward to your findings.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'll... I'll do my best to find the answers. I hope the information I find helps us make a safe choice that won't cause problems for anyone later. I'm looking forward to hearing what you all find.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Sakura,,Yay! I'm super ready to go on this treasure hunt for information! I'll find out all the secrets about the plants and the team. See you all soon with the juicy details! Bye-bye!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I will proceed with my investigation. I intend to bring objective data regarding our daily losses to the table, ensuring our decision is based on reality rather than how impressive a proposal sounds.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Asuka,,I will proceed as well. I intend to determine if our human resources are being treated as an infinite resource or if we actually have the capacity to handle the workload. I will report my findings shortly.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
