35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"My research reveals a clear pattern: broad, demanding projects often fade away, while narrow, specialized tools for specific trades endure. We must seek a solution that is focused and sustainable, rather than one that asks too much.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I found that the capital budget is actually frozen. Only the recurring software allowance has room. Also, per-head licenses get more expensive as we expand, while fixed-fee work is more stable. We should be very careful about license costs.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Oh boy, we have a big problem! Half the plants lose signal in the afternoons, and getting device approval takes forever! Plus, the coordination group is basically just two poor people doing everything by hand. We're totally stuck!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"My findings confirm significant daily waste. We lose nearly two hours every day to redundant data copying, and misrouted deliveries are occurring due to inconsistent address records across units. These are systemic, recurring losses that we must address.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The situation is worse than I feared. Our in-house developers are fully committed until Q3, and the previous integrator left us with undocumented interfaces. We have no technical bandwidth to support a complex new implementation right now.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"It seems we are all facing a sobering reality. @Asuka and @Sakura, your findings on staffing and infrastructure suggest that any grand ambition would be a burden. We must look for a small, focused victory.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree with @Servas. Since the capital budget is frozen, we can't afford anything that requires a large upfront investment. We should look for a project that fits within the software allowance and avoids expensive per-head licenses.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"Exactly! If we pick something that needs a fancy new app, it'll just crash when the signal disappears, and those two poor people in coordination will have to fix it by hand! We need something super simple!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Sakura, simplicity is a requirement, but it must be targeted. The data shows we are bleeding time through redundant copying and address errors. Any proposal that ignores these specific, daily losses is merely a cosmetic improvement.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, targeting those losses is logical, but we must be realistic. With our developers unavailable until Q3 and undocumented interfaces, any project requiring deep technical integration is a non-starter. We cannot afford to overload the remaining staff.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,"It is a delicate balance we must strike. We need a solution that addresses @Ryuji's operational waste, yet remains small enough to survive @Asuka's staffing shortage and @Daisuke's budget constraints. A narrow, specialized tool is our safest path.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Asuka"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think @Servas is right. If we choose a project with a fixed-fee structure instead of per-head licenses, it won't suddenly become unaffordable next year. We really need to avoid any hidden costs that could surprise us later.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"And we can't forget the plants! If the project needs a constant internet connection or new devices, it's going to be a total disaster. We need something that works even when the signal goes poof! Right?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Sakura, correct. A solution that relies on unstable connectivity is a failure by design. However, we must not let these constraints lead us to a project that does nothing. We need a tool that specifically eliminates the redundant copying and address discrepancies.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, I agree that we need a tool that works, but not at the cost of a total burnout. If a proposal requires heavy developer support or manual data cleanup, it will fail regardless of its intent.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Servas,,"We have reached a consensus on our constraints. We require a project that is narrow in scope, avoids high license fees, functions despite poor connectivity, and demands minimal developer time. Let us now see which candidate fits this humble yet sturdy mold.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I hope the candidates have some options that fit. I'll be looking for the one that is most financially stable and doesn't rely on that frozen capital budget. I just want us to be safe.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Sakura,,"I'm with you, Daisuke! I'll be cheering for the project that doesn't need a magic internet connection or a million people to run it. Let's find the one that actually works in the real world!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I will support the candidate that directly targets the redundant data entry and address inconsistencies. If a proposal solves these specific, measurable losses without requiring heavy infrastructure, it is the only rational choice.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"I will support the proposal that requires the least amount of internal manpower. Given our developer shortage and the burden on the coordination group, any project demanding significant staff time is an unacceptable risk.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
